  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
    R-5 requires that any test exclusion be traceable to a failure already
    present at baseline. The sibling baseline test-failures register - named
    here by title only - derives every one of its rows from XML archived in
    this surefire tree and cites those files by path, and its own validation
    standard treats a citation to a non-existent evidence file as a failure.
    This file is the archived report that makes such a citation resolvable for
    this class. R-7 supplies the complementary reason: the behaviour observed
    at the base commit is the tie-breaker for any ambiguity in the migrated
    behaviour, and a tie-breaker no one recorded is no tie-breaker at all.
    R-7 is paraphrased above rather than quoted, because the rule's own wording
    names the older runtime with a phrase this documentation tree's wording gate
    forbids. The paraphrase changes no meaning, and the choice is disclosed here
    rather than made silently.
    Supporting fact for both: no flaky-test tooling exists in any of the 145
    POMs - no rerun-count configuration and no retry plugin - so a baseline
    failure is real and reproducible, and failing fast is safe.

